    "bellaRecommendation": [
      "Read each owning object's complete OMFI:MOBJ:MobID value using its dictionary type, declared width and applicable metadata byte order.",
      "Preserve and compare the complete normalized32-byte identity for modern IDs.",
      "Normalize all three words of a12-byte UID. For the verified organization42 family, use its reversible Avid wrapper to match legacy/modern PMR identities.",
      "For another organization, retain the complete normalized12-byte UID with a distinct format/namespace. Do not discard its first word or claim an unproven PMR join.",
      "Use owner role and reference relationships to distinguish FileMobId and MasterMobId; the property name is the same. An object handle or an auxiliary index UID is not a replacement for the owning object's actual identity.",
      "Normalize each source once, then compare complete identities. Never use an eight-byte excerpt for modern identity matching or try arbitrary whole-ID byte reversals.",
      "This follows the existing approved complete-ID requirement. It does not change KelpieId, duplicate inventory rules or the Bin Filter."
    ],
    "coverageAndLimits": [
      "The actual same-machine little-endian corpus match is separately recorded by the team; this task establishes native structure and conversion paths.",
      "No genuine big-endian PMR/MDB specimen was exercised. Native code establishes exact transformations; future verification still needs genuine or appropriately identified authored endian cases.",
      "The existing OldScanner canonicalDatabaseId helper normalizes8/12-byte big-endian IDs but passes32 bytes through unchanged. Do not reuse that limitation as Bella policy; no production helper was changed.",
      "Unknown widths, unreadable required references and general MDB damage policy remain separate requirements. This research does not invent new damaged-ID prefix tests."
    ],
